From: syabyr <syabyr@github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: multi: default to a removable LUN

g_multi bound at boot as a built-in driver has no file= module
parameter, so fsg_common_create_lun() rejects the empty default LUN
with -EINVAL ("no file given for LUN0") and the whole composite
gadget fails to bind to the UDC:

    udc fcc00000.usb: failed to start g_multi: -22
    UDC core: g_multi: couldn't find an available UDC

Make the default LUN removable so the gadget binds with an empty
(no medium) LUN, matching how g_multi is normally loaded as a module
with removable=1.  An explicit file= parameter still overrides it.

Signed-off-by: syabyr <syabyr@github.com>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/multi.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/multi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/multi.c
@@ -104,7 +104,10 @@
 /****************************** Configurations ******************************/

-static struct fsg_module_parameters fsg_mod_data = { .stall = 1 };
+static struct fsg_module_parameters fsg_mod_data = {
+	.stall = 1,
+	.removable = { [0 ... FSG_MAX_LUNS - 1] = 1 },
+};
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_GADGET_DEBUG_FILES

 static unsigned int fsg_num_buffers = CONFIG_USB_GADGET_STORAGE_NUM_BUFFERS;
